  "description_html": "<p>A fossil <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeopteryx\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Archaeopteryx\">Archaeopteryx</a> Lithographica, taken on 2007-05-18 in the <i>Staatliches Museum für Naturkunde</i> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karlsruhe\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Karlsruhe\">Karlsruhe</a>, Germany. This is claimed to be the well-preserved Thermopolis specimen.<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.vdbiol.de/vdbiol/content/e5/e224/index_ger.html?news_id=4175\">[1]</a><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.smnk.de/SMNK/04-0-Aktuelles.html\">[2]</a><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.natur.de/scripts/basics/eco-world/service/events/basics.prg?session=42f94645464f3593_2001&amp;nap=natur&amp;a_no=3296&amp;main=drucken\">[3]</a>\n</p><p>Image taken by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Stephan_Schulz\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:User:Stephan Schulz\">User:Stephan Schulz</a>.\n</p><p>Since I'm not a photo expert, I've uploaded the images as raw as possible, i.e. without any correction for colour, horizon, or angle. Feel free to improve them.\n</p>\nThe caption in the museum described this specimen as \"probably found in in Eichstätt, Frankenalb, Bavaria, Germany\", and from the upper <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jurassic\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Jurassic\">Jurassic</a>, 150 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega-annum\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Mega-annum\">Ma</a>.",
